course: dictionary
lesson: 3146
title: Feeling embarrassed
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Embarrassed means feeling shy, awkward or a bit ashamed, often because something happened in front of other people. Your face may go red and you may want to hide. «She's embarrassed, and also weirdly relieved she's not the only one.» The word «also» tells you she feels two things at once, and the word «relieved» means she feels better.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «A girl in Dublin was so embarrassed after falling over on stage that she refused to go to school for three days.» Falling over on stage is something that happens in front of people, and refusing to go to school shows how bad she felt. So embarrassed must mean feeling shy and ashamed.
explain: Embarrassed can also be the past of the verb embarrass. To embarrass someone is to make them feel this way. Check with the sentence: if you can put «made him feel embarrassed» in its place and it still makes sense, you have the verb meaning.
explain: Everyone feels embarrassed sometimes. «A real friend protects you when you are embarrassed, by being kind, not by hurting anyone else.» Being kind is the right way to help someone who is embarrassed.
fact: Embarrassed means feeling shy, awkward or a bit ashamed in front of other people.
fact: Embarrassed is also the past of embarrass: to embarrass someone is to make them feel this way.
fact: Everyone feels embarrassed sometimes, for example after tripping in the playground or giving a wrong answer.
fact: You can say embarrassed about something, or embarrassed to say something, as in «embarrassed to say» a secret you feel shy about.
fact: Don't laugh at someone who is embarrassed; being kind helps them feel better.
exercise: «A girl in Dublin was so embarrassed after falling over on stage that she refused to go to school for three days.» What does embarrassed mean here? | Very angry with the stage | *Shy and ashamed because of what happened in front of people | Hungry and tired after a long day | Happy and proud of her big fall
exercise: Ben looked down and his face went red after his wrong answer. Which word fits the gap: Ben was ___? | curt | barely | *embarrassed | ancient
exercise: A friend says «It's nothing» after a fall, because they are embarrassed. What is a kind thing to do? | Laugh and tell everyone in the playground | Make them tell the whole class what happened | *Say nothing about it and do not laugh | Shout at them to get up quickly
test: Which sentence uses embarrassed as the past of embarrass? | The joke embarrassed him in front of everyone. | She felt embarrassed about her new haircut. | He was embarrassed to say he had lost his bag. | *The joke embarrassed him, so he went red and looked down.
test: «She's embarrassed, and also weirdly relieved she's not the only one.» What does this tell you? | She is hungry and wants her lunch | She is happy and has won a prize | She is angry and wants to shout at everyone | *She feels shy and ashamed, but she is glad she is not alone in it
exam: A friend trips and feels embarrassed. Which of these is the best way to help them? | *Be kind, and do not hurt them or make a fuss | Tell the whole school about it at once | Walk away and never speak to them again | Laugh loudly so everyone knows what happened
